## Outcomes

Every scanned unit is exactly one of these, so the rows **conserve to the total** —
reducing one bucket (e.g. eliminating timeouts) just moves those units into the
others. Read the two **bold** group rows for the verdict; the indented rows break
them down (a single sub-row moving isn't independently good or bad).

| | base | head | Δ |
|---|---|---|---|
| ✅ **correct** (TP + TN) | {{ base.confusion.correct }} | {{ head.confusion.correct }} | {{ (head.confusion.correct - base.confusion.correct) | delta(as_int=true) }} |
| &emsp;true positives · malware caught | {{ base.confusion.tp }} | {{ head.confusion.tp }} | {{ (head.confusion.tp - base.confusion.tp) | signed }} |
| &emsp;true negatives · benign passed | {{ base.confusion.tn }} | {{ head.confusion.tn }} | {{ (head.confusion.tn - base.confusion.tn) | signed }} |
